      {
        "kind": "faq",
        "title": "Frequently asked questions",
        "items": [
          {
            "question": "What is an electronic signature and digital signature?",
            "answer": "Electronic signatures (eSignatures): a more general term for fast and secure ways to sign online agreements. It usually includes needing to do actions like typing your name and uploading your signature, and can include drawing a signature with a mouse or finger.\n\nDigital signatures: a more specific term than eSignature, which has an extra layer of security. Usually, this happens via encryption and identity verification. Most advanced eSignature tools, such as Assembly, use digital signature technology to keep your documents compliant and secure."
          },
          {
            "question": "Are eSignatures legally enforceable?",
            "answer": "Yes. eSignatures are legally enforceable and valid in most countries, such as the U.S. and countries within the EU.\n\nWhen a client signs a contract in Assembly, it includes a full audit trail; you will have clear proof of who signed what, when they signed it, and where they were when it happened."
          },
          {
            "question": "What types of documents can be signed electronically?",
            "answer": "You can use Assembly to sign things the following: client agreements (like MSAs and SOWs), freelance or contractor agreements, NDAs, proposals, onboarding forms, and more.\n\nIf you can upload it as a PDF, you can sign it with Assembly."
          },
          {
            "question": "What document formats do Assembly contracts support?",
            "answer": "Assembly supports PDF contracts. This keeps your formatting consistent across devices and is the industry standard digital signatures."
          },
          {
            "question": "How do recipients sign Assembly contracts?",
            "answer": "Clients receive a contract directly through your branded client portal or via email. No logins or downloads are required in order to sign. Just click, review, and sign. Signing the contract is easy to do and optimized for desktop and mobile."
          },
          {
            "question": "How do I know if a recipient has signed a contract?",
            "answer": "You will get updated when your client signs a contract. You'll see the updated contract status in your dashboard as soon as it's signed. Your client can also view a final copy of the signed contract in their portal."
          },
          {
            "question": "How is Assembly different from DocuSign, HelloSign, PandaDoc, and others?",
            "answer": "Assembly isn’t just for contracts—it is a full client experience platform complete with a CRM and client portal.\n\nTools like DocuSign focus solely on signatures, but Assembly brings together contracts, payments, messaging, forms, file-sharing, and more into one client portal.\n\nAssembly's Advanced plan is white-labeled, so your brand stays front and center—on your domain, in your emails, and throughout the client experience.\n\nYour clients get one simple login for everything. You get a streamlined, professional workflow that scales."
          }
        ]
      }
